se / Who Cares? update or Eurostat SES round).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Kills CQ1's second conjunct on a six-year read of an eleven-year race: +10.0 pp by 2036 would then need ~1.6 pp/yr for five years. CQ1 falls from 26 to ~10; confirms the one-sided composition argument was in fact correctly signed and my within-F+Q upward composition claim was wrong.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"G7 GDP-weighted 10-year sovereign real yield averages below 1.20% over any rolling 24-month period in which no G7 member records two consecutive quarters of negative real GDP growth (i.e. a low-real-yield regime without a recession).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my repression-reversal claim and shows the wedge is a standing capacity rather than a regime artifact. CQ4 P50 falls from 2.50 to ~1.85 and P90 from 3.90 to ~3.1; CQ5 conjunct A falls from 0.55 to ~0.36, taking CQ5 from 26 to ~16; and the r-g constraint then argues my CQ3 is too high by ~0.2 pp.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 2 premortem seat, effort 'labor'."}}